SUMMARY:Sack of potatoes - run + circuit mix
DESCRIPTION:Leader: Joe de la Mata\n\nThis is a bit of a different run to k
 ick off with my run leading for the buzzards!\n\n5K road run starting with 
 a quick warm up and ending with some cool-down stretches. At half way (Vict
 oria Park) we will break for a short set of circuit mix exercises to boost 
 our running performance and improve our form (e.g. squats\, jumps\, and a b
 it of upper core exercises like lateral raises). It’ll be really fun\, I 
 promise!\n\nLevel: intermediate. Don’t be put off by the idea of doing th
 e exercises\, as long as you are happy to do a 5K you should be able to do 
 the exercises too (as they will be adapted if you have any injuries/difficu
 lties).\n\nRoute: ~5K circular route at conversational pace starting from P
 riory Park to Victoria Park via Link Common and back. \n\nMeet-up point: by
  the entrance to Priory Park where Malvern Splash is at.\n\nThe route is ca
 lled Sack of potatoes as the shape in the map reminds me to it. There must 
 be about 11 potatoes inside (you will only get the reference if you were at
  the AGM!).\n\nJoe - [Phone Number Redacted]\n\nView on Strava: https://www
 .strava.com/clubs/208705/group_events/3457333727823422612\n\nSynced from St
 rava Club 208705 on Sat\, 21 Feb @ 3:22 AM
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:Leader: Joe de la MataThis is a bit of a diffe
 rent run to kick off with my run leading for the buzzards!5K road run start
 ing with a quick warm up and ending with some cool-down stretches. At half 
 way (Victoria Park) we will break for a short set of circuit mix exercises 
 to boost our running performance and improve our form (e.g. squats\, jumps\
 , and a bit of upper core exercises like lateral raises). It’ll be really
  fun\, I promise!Level: intermediate. Don’t be put off by the idea of doi
 ng the exercises\, as long as you are happy to do a 5K you should be able t
 o do the exercises too (as they will be adapted if you have any injuries/di
 fficulties).Route: ~5K circular route at conversational pace starting from 
 Priory Park to Victoria Park via Link Common and back. Meet-up point: by th
 e entrance to Priory Park where Malvern Splash is at.The route is called Sa
 ck of potatoes as the shape in the map reminds me to it. There must be abou
 t 11 potatoes inside (you will only get the reference if you were at the AG
 M!).Joe - [Phone Number Redacted]View on Strava: https://www.strava.com/clu
 bs/208705/group_events/3457333727823422612Synced from Strava Club 208705 on
 : Sat\, 21 Feb @ 3:22 AM
LOCATION:8 Priory Road Malvern England WR14 United Kingdom
URL:https://www.strava.com/clubs/208705/group_events/3457333727823422612
